# IT Work TV — Cloudflare Pages _redirects
#
# PURPOSE: content moves only. A 301 is appended to this file when a PUBLISHED
# URL is renamed. Nothing else belongs here.
#
# FORMAT: one redirect per line, "from to status". Blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored by Pages.
#
# 1. NO www -> apex rule goes in this file. Domain-level redirects are
#    explicitly NOT supported in Pages _redirects (verified 2026-10-04,
#    https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/).
#    www.itworktv.com -> itworktv.com is a Cloudflare ZONE-LEVEL Redirect
#    Rule created in the dashboard — see docs/SETUP.md, step 4.
# 2. NO host of any kind in "from" or "to". No https:// rule, no apex rule,
#    no cross-domain rule. Paths only.
#
# WHEN A PUBLISHED SLUG IS RENAMED (PLAN §3.2 / §5.2 rule 6: renaming is the
# only event, and it is a 301, never a delete), append one line plus a dated
# comment so qa-auditor can confirm the destination still exists in the
# sitemap:
#
#   /posts/<old-slug>/  /posts/<new-slug>/  301   # 2026-11-01: renamed <old> -> <new>
#
# Rules: status is always 301 (never 302). The old URL keeps serving until
# the new URL is fully indexed, so entries are rarely, if ever, deleted.
# Cap: 2,100 rules total (PLAN §10.6) — we will use single digits.
#
# (Intentionally empty for now: the site has published zero URLs yet.)
